	(text "Interlock (hardware, independent of firmware):\n  TMC_DRV_ENN = NAND(DRV_EN, E_OK)      -> driver off unless the MCU enables it AND E-stop loop closed\n  CLUTCH_*    = AND(MCU request, E_OK)  -> clutch off on E-stop\nMCU outputs have pull-downs so everything is off while the RP2040 is in reset.\nE-stop: NC contact between ESTOP_SRC (+3V3 via 330R) and ESTOP_RET. Open or broken wire -> E_OK low.\nThe MCU only reads E_OK through 100k (E_OK_SENSE), so firmware can never hold the interlock enabled.\nThe E-stop removes driver enable and clutch drive; it does not disconnect the 36 V bus.\nRP2040 per Raspberry Pi's minimal design: 12 MHz crystal (1k series), W25Q128JV QSPI flash (firmware uses 2 MB), internal\n1.1 V core regulator. GPIO numbers are the ones the old Pico module used, so the firmware is unchanged.\n+3V3: AP2112K from VSYS = +5V or USB VBUS through Schottkys (USB alone powers the logic for flashing).\nFlash a blank board: hold BOOTSEL, tap RESET, copy the UF2. SWD on a 1x3 0.1in header: SWCLK, GND, SWDIO (Debug Probe pinout)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
